{{Quote|Missiles. Pull up!''"<br />"''They overshot us.|[[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], during the [[Battle of Coruscant]]|<ref name="Episode 3">{{Film|III}}</ref>}}
[[File:Missiles-SWGoH.png|250px|thumb|right|A trio of missiles]]
A '''missile''', sometimes called a '''rocket''', was an explosive projectile that was fired from some type of [[missile launcher]]. Missiles were used in both space combat and ground warfare. Missile launchers were equipped on vehicles and [[starship]]s such as the [[HMP droid gunship|droid gunship]]<ref name="Databank Droid Gunship">{{Databank|droid-gunship|Droid Gunship}}</ref> and the [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry|Republic Attack Gunship]].<ref name="Databank Republic attack gunship">{{Databank|republic-attack-gunship|Republic Attack Gunship}}</ref> They were also used by [[battle droid]]s, [[clone trooper]]s,<ref name="Ambush EG">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/ambush-episode-gallery|text="Ambush" Episode Gallery}} {{C|Slide 9}}</ref> and [[Mandalorian warrior]]s.<ref name="The Mandalore Plot EG">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-mandalore-plot-episode-gallery|text="The Mandalore Plot" Episode Gallery}} {{C|Slides 9 and 15}}</ref> Examples of missiles include [[proton torpedo]]es, [[concussion missile]]s, and [[discord missile]]s.<ref name="Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

Missile weapons were considered a complement to [[blaster]]s and other energy weapons because of their unique characteristics. Missiles were capable of homing in on a target, even moving around intervening obstacles in order to hit it. Thanks to the use of [[acceleration compensator]]s and [[tensor field]]s, missiles could withstand turning accelerations of up to 10,000 G, such as when making a 90-degree turn within a turning radius of one meter. When fired from a planetary surface they could hit a target that was hidden by the horizon. Missiles could also follow a preprogrammed trajectory or receive targeting updates via encrypted guidance signals, transmitted by either forward observers or orbiting craft.<ref name="Complete Vehicles" />

However, missiles were much easier to dodge than blasters and were vulnerable to being shot down.<ref name="Complete Vehicles">''[[Star Wars Complete Vehicles, New Edition]]''</ref> Some missiles took deliberately evasive flight paths or otherwise used their agility to avoid being shot down.<ref name="Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref><ref name="Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> Missiles were also vulnerable to a number of [[electronic countermeasures]] such as [[sensor jammer]]s, [[XX-5 Seeker Warhead|seeker warhead]]s, [[chaff]], and [[Sensor Inverter]]s.<ref name="Star Wars: Squadrons">''[[Star Wars: Squadrons]]''</ref>

Missiles could be fitted with a variety of different [[warhead]]s, such as [[Proton warhead|proton]], [[Electromagnetic pulse|EMP]], [[Antimatter/Canon|antimatter]], or hard [[radiation]], depending on the needs of the mission. Missile warheads could have variable yields, and the resulting explosion could be omnidirectional or focused in a particular direction. The missiles used by Republic attack gunships, for example, concentrated their explosion in a two-degree cone.<ref name="Complete Vehicles" />

[[File:Rocket_Launch_SWB.png|thumb|left|250px|A missile being fired from a missile launcher]]
Missiles came in a variety of sizes with corresponding differences in their destructive potential. A [[A/SF-01 B-wing starfighter|B-wing]] could carry missiles powerful enough that their shock waves would knock whole groups of starfighters out of the sky if used in an atmosphere.<ref name="Alphabet Squadron (novel)">[[Alphabet Squadron (novel)|''Alphabet Squadron'']]</ref> [[Capital ship]]-scale missiles like those carried by [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyers]] could cause explosions big enough to boil lakes or collapse [[mountain]]-sized factories,<ref name="Shadow Fall">''[[Shadow Fall: An Alphabet Squadron Novel]]''</ref> while proton torpedoes like those carried on [[Acclamator-class transgalactic military assault ship|''Acclamator''-class assault ships]] were used in [[Base Delta Zero]] bombardments which could melt the upper crust of a planet.<ref name="Complete Vehicles" /> In the [[Battle of Umbara]], the [[Umbaran Militia]] utilized long-range missiles with 100-[[Metric ton|megaton]] warheads (supplied by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatists]]) to defend their capital from the [[Grand Army of the Republic]].<ref name="SW-Plan of Dissent Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/plan-of-dissent-episode-guide|text="Plan of Dissent" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref>

